# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/

# Node
js/node_modules/
js/npm_install.log

# Environment build artifacts (the lockfile IS committed)
env/build.log

# Large run artifacts — manifests and resolved configs are re-included below.
#
# 2026-08-17: `runs/adapters/` never matched anything. The real trees are
# `runs/adapters_srh/` and `runs/adapters_cft/`, so 53 GB of LoRA weights sat UNIGNORED and
# `git add -A` would have committed all of it. Globbed now so a new `adapters_<thread>/`
# tree is covered the day it appears. CLAUDE.md §2 requires these to be gitignored; the
# rule was stated but not enforced.
runs/adapters/
runs/adapters_*/
runs/trace_cache/
runs/candidates/
# 2026-09-23: the SAME defect as the 2026-08-17 note above, found while preparing a handoff
# commit. `runs/mole/` (learned-router expert banks + gate.pt) and `runs/merges/` (merged
# adapter weights) were never matched by any rule, so ~800 MB of weights sat UNIGNORED and a
# `git add -A` would have committed all of it. Globbed by weight-bearing tree, and
# run_manifest.json is still re-included below so provenance survives.
runs/mole/
runs/merges/
runs/taskvecs/
runs/align_cache/
runs/probe/
runs/pipeline/
runs/logs/
runs/manifest/running/
runs/manifest/.supervisor.lock
results/cells/
results/attn/
results/forgetting/*.parquet
results/*.parquet
results/**/*.parquet
# Raw per-trial generations. One eval pass is 40-95 MB and the whole tree is ~800 MB, which
# is a large artifact under CLAUDE.md §2. The derived files beside them (summary.json,
# contrasts.*, metric_tables.md, run_manifest.json) ARE committed and are what a result is
# read from; trials.jsonl is only needed to recompute them.
results/**/trials.jsonl
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.npz
*.pt

# Keep the reproducibility record
!runs/**/run_manifest.json
!results/**/cell_meta.json
!results/analysis/*.json
!results/attn/SCHEMA.md

# Scratch
*.log
.DS_Store

# Vendored tool BINARIES. `env/vendor/` (codebleu) is committed because it is pure Python and
# small; a compiled platform-specific executable is a different kind of thing and does not
# belong in history. The dist-info beside it records the exact pin (py_spy 0.4.2), so the tool
# stays reproducible via pip without carrying a 7.7 MB blob.
env/vendor_tools/bin/

# A SEPARATE PROJECT THAT LIVES IN THIS DIRECTORY BUT IS NOT PART OF IT.
# `LLM-Attention-Fixation_gitready/` appeared in the repo root on 2026-09-14 and a `git add -A`
# swept all 8,211 of its files into commit e6617e0 and pushed them. It is someone else's codebase,
# it carries an anonymous-artifact mirror URL, and 37 MB of it does not belong in obtune's history.
# Ignored so no future `add -A` can repeat that. The files stay on disk, untouched.
LLM-Attention-Fixation_gitready/

# Submission archives for the OTHER project that shares this directory. `ase2026.zip` is 246 MB and
# `LLM-Attention-Fixation.zip` 14 MB; both appeared on 2026-09-14 alongside the directory above.
# Checked while looking for the paper's undefined `ase26` citation: the archive holds that project's
# own ASE submission (Model_Steering.pdf, the attention-steering work), NOT the Rong et al. paper
# intro-2.tex cites. So it does not resolve that reference, and it must not enter this history.
ase2026.zip
LLM-Attention-Fixation.zip
